No rights are granted except those expressly stated in this License.

3. COMMERCIAL USE

Commercial Use is not permitted under this License.

A separate written commercial license from the Licensor is required before the RIBOSPAN Model Materials, Derivative Models, Separable Adaptations, Output-Derived Models, Outputs, or Output Derivatives are used for Commercial Use.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

3.1 Commercial Products and Services

Use in connection with any product, platform, technology, or service that is sold, licensed, subscribed to, monetized, or otherwise provided for commercial consideration.

3.2 Hosted Models, APIs, and Analysis Services

Providing access to RIBOSPAN, a Derivative Model, a Separable Adaptation, an Output-Derived Model, or Outputs generated using any of them by means of:

(a) a commercial API;

(b) software-as-a-service;

(c) hosted inference;

(d) cloud services;

(e) paid analysis services;

(f) commercial sequence-scoring services;

(g) commercial embedding or representation services;

(h) commercial sequence-design or optimization services; or

(i) other commercial model-serving, prediction, analytical, or computational arrangements.

3.3 Commercial Research and Development

Use by, on behalf of, or primarily for the benefit of a for-profit entity in research or development materially directed toward a current or future commercial product, service, platform, technology, development program, or commercially exploitable intellectual property.

3.4 Sponsored Research, Contract Research, and Consulting

Research, development, consulting, testing, validation, optimization, or other work performed primarily for the commercial benefit of a third party, including work carried out under a commercial sponsorship, contract research agreement, service agreement, consulting agreement, or similar arrangement.

3.5 Biotechnology and Life-Science Development

Use in the discovery, screening, scoring, selection, ranking, optimization, validation, development, manufacture, regulatory development, or commercialization of any of the following for commercial purposes:

(a) therapeutics;

(b) vaccines;

(c) diagnostics;

(d) RNA medicines;

(e) nucleic-acid products;

(f) biotechnology products;

(g) agricultural biotechnology products;

(h) industrial biotechnology products; or

(i) other biological products, technologies, or services.

3.6 Commercial Exploitation of Model-Assisted Designs

Commercial exploitation of nucleotide sequences, biological molecules, candidate designs, optimized sequences, selected variants, or other biological or technological results where their selection, prioritization, optimization, modification, design, or development was materially enabled by or based on use of the RIBOSPAN Model Materials, a Derivative Model, a Separable Adaptation, an Output-Derived Model, or Outputs.

For clarity, this Section does not transfer ownership of independently owned user inputs or independently owned intellectual property to the Licensor.

3.7 Commercial Use of Output-Derived Models

Commercial deployment, licensing, sale, distribution for commercial purposes, hosted use, or internal commercial use of an Output-Derived Model materially developed using RIBOSPAN Outputs or representations requires a separate written commercial license from the Licensor.

3.8 Internal Commercial Use

Use of RIBOSPAN, a Derivative Model, a Separable Adaptation, an Output-Derived Model, Outputs, or Output Derivatives within an internal workflow of a commercial entity constitutes Commercial Use where such use materially supports:

(a) a commercial product;

(b) a commercial service;

(c) a commercial research or development program;

(d) commercial decision-making;

(e) intellectual-property generation directed toward commercial exploitation; or

(f) another revenue-generating or commercially strategic activity.

4. DERIVATIVE MODELS

You may create Derivative Models solely for purposes permitted under this License.

Derivative Models remain subject to this License to the extent that their creation, use, modification, or distribution depends upon rights granted under this License.

Modification of the RIBOSPAN Model Materials does not grant any additional commercial rights.

You may not avoid or circumvent the restrictions of this License by fine-tuning, continued pretraining, quantizing, merging, converting, adapting, pruning, or otherwise modifying the Model Materials.

Subject to Sections 9, 10, and 11, Derivative Models and permitted Separable Adaptations may be modified, shared, and redistributed for Non-Commercial Research Purposes in accordance with this License.

Commercial Use of a Derivative Model or Separable Adaptation developed from the RIBOSPAN Model Materials requires a separate written commercial license from the Licensor.

5. MODEL DISTILLATION, EXTRACTION, AND SUBSTITUTE MODELS

Except with prior written permission from the Licensor, you may not use the RIBOSPAN Model Materials, Derivative Models, Separable Adaptations, Output-Derived Models, Outputs, or Output Derivatives for any of the following activities.

5.1 Model Distillation

You may not perform model distillation, imitation learning, teacher-student training, or substantially similar procedures intended to transfer substantial RIBOSPAN capabilities into another general-purpose model.

5.2 Model Extraction

You may not systematically query, process, or evaluate RIBOSPAN for the purpose of extracting, reconstructing, approximating, or reproducing substantial capabilities or behavior of RIBOSPAN.

5.3 Training Substitute Foundation Models

You may not systematically generate, collect, or curate RIBOSPAN Outputs or Output Derivatives for the purpose of training, pretraining, optimizing, or materially improving a general-purpose RNA foundation model or another model intended to reproduce or substitute for substantial capabilities of RIBOSPAN.

5.4 Competing General-Purpose Models

You may not use the RIBOSPAN Model Materials, Derivative Models, Separable Adaptations, Output-Derived Models, Outputs, or Output Derivatives to create or materially improve a model intended to serve as a substantially similar general-purpose replacement for RIBOSPAN.

5.5 Permitted Task-Specific Downstream Models

This Section does not prohibit the development of task-specific Derivative Models, Separable Adaptations, or Output-Derived Models for specialized Non-Commercial Research Purposes, including:

(a) classification;

(b) regression;

(c) functional annotation;

(d) structure prediction;

(e) localization prediction;

(f) sequence-property prediction;

(g) variant analysis; or

(h) other specialized scientific tasks,

provided that such models or adaptations are not intended to reproduce or substitute for RIBOSPAN as a general-purpose RNA foundation model and are otherwise used in compliance with this License.

6. OUTPUTS, OUTPUT DERIVATIVES, AND OUTPUT-DERIVED MODELS

You may generate and use Outputs and Output Derivatives, and develop and use Output-Derived Models, for Non-Commercial Research Purposes.

Subject to Sections 10 and 11, Output-Derived Models may be modified, shared, and redistributed for Non-Commercial Research Purposes in accordance with this License.

Commercial Use of Outputs, Output Derivatives, or Output-Derived Models materially resulting from use of the RIBOSPAN Model Materials requires a separate written commercial license from the Licensor.

Examples include, without limitation, commercial use of:

(a) model-ranked RNA sequences;

(b) model-optimized nucleotide sequences;

(c) model-selected variants;

(d) model-assisted molecular or sequence designs;

(e) embeddings incorporated into commercial systems;

(f) sequence scores used in commercial research or decision-making;

(g) candidate molecules or sequences materially selected using RIBOSPAN;

(h) task-specific models materially trained or developed using RIBOSPAN embeddings, hidden representations, predictions, scores, or other Outputs; or

(i) other RIBOSPAN-assisted models, designs, selections, or decisions used in commercial development.

7. USER INPUTS

You retain whatever rights you may have in data, sequences, molecules, designs, or other materials that you provide as input to RIBOSPAN.

Processing, embedding, scoring, predicting, ranking, or evaluating an input using RIBOSPAN does not, by itself, transfer ownership of that input to the Licensor.

An independently owned input does not become owned by the Licensor, nor does its underlying ownership change, merely because RIBOSPAN has processed it.

Nothing in this Section exempts the use of RIBOSPAN-generated scores, rankings, selections, embeddings, predictions, optimization results, or other Outputs from the restrictions of this License.

Where commercial selection, prioritization, optimization, modification, validation, or development of a user-owned input materially relies on RIBOSPAN Outputs, such use constitutes Commercial Use to the extent described in Section 3.

8. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY IN OUTPUTS

Nothing in this License determines whether copyright, patent, database, trade-secret, or other intellectual property rights arise in any particular Output, Output Derivative, Output-Derived Model, Derivative Model, or Separable Adaptation, or who owns such rights under applicable law.

The contractual restrictions imposed by this License apply independently of whether a particular Output, Output Derivative, Output-Derived Model, Derivative Model, or Separable Adaptation is eligible for copyright, patent, or other intellectual property protection.

Nothing in this License transfers ownership of independently owned user inputs, independently developed materials, or independently owned third-party intellectual property to the Licensor.

Nothing in this Section grants a user any rights in patents, trademarks, copyrights, trade secrets, datasets, biological materials, or other intellectual property owned or controlled by the Licensor except as expressly provided by this License.

