11. RESTRICTED-ACCESS CHECKPOINTS

A Restricted-Access Checkpoint is subject to the additional restrictions in this Section.

11.1 No Redistribution

You may not redistribute, transfer, publish, mirror, upload, share, or otherwise provide a Restricted-Access Checkpoint to another person or legal entity without prior written permission from the Licensor.

11.2 Independent Access Requirement

Each person or legal entity seeking access to a Restricted-Access Checkpoint must obtain access independently through an official distribution channel designated by the Licensor.

11.3 No Access-Sharing

You may not share authentication tokens, accounts, credentials, private download links, access keys, or other access mechanisms that permit another person or legal entity to access a Restricted-Access Checkpoint.

11.4 Models and Adaptations Developed from Restricted-Access Checkpoints

You may not distribute, without prior written permission from the Licensor, any full, merged, or otherwise self-contained Derivative Model created from or materially based on a Restricted-Access Checkpoint, including any full checkpoint produced through fine-tuning, continued pretraining, quantization, pruning, model conversion, model merging, or similar modification of a Restricted-Access Checkpoint. This restriction applies regardless of whether the parameters of the resulting Derivative Model are numerically identical to the parameters of the original Restricted-Access Checkpoint.

For Non-Commercial Research Purposes, you may distribute Separable Adaptations developed from a Restricted-Access Checkpoint, including task-specific adapters, LoRA parameters, parameter-efficient fine-tuning modules, task-specific heads, or similar separable components, provided that:

(a) the distributed materials do not include the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint or a substantial portion of its model parameters;

(b) the distributed materials cannot reasonably be used by themselves to reconstruct, reproduce, or substitute for the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint;

(c) where use of the distributed Separable Adaptation requires the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint, each recipient must obtain access to that checkpoint independently through an official distribution channel designated by the Licensor;

(d) the Separable Adaptation is intended for a specialized downstream task and is not intended to reproduce, approximate, substitute for, or materially replicate substantial general-purpose capabilities of RIBOSPAN;

(e) the distributor clearly identifies the Restricted-Access RIBOSPAN checkpoint from which the Separable Adaptation was developed;

(f) the distributor prominently states, in the model card, README, repository page, or other primary distribution documentation, that the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint is not provided with the Separable Adaptation and must be independently obtained from an official RIBOSPAN distribution channel designated by the Licensor, and provides a clear reference to the applicable RIBOSPAN checkpoint and this License;

(g) reasonable attribution to RIBOSPAN is provided;

(h) the distribution includes a copy of, or a clear reference to, this License, and recipients are clearly informed that use of the Separable Adaptation and access to and use of the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint remain subject to the applicable terms of this License;

(i) the distribution does not include substantial collections of Outputs prohibited under Section 11.5; and

(j) the distribution otherwise complies with this License.

For clarity, the preceding paragraph permits, for Non-Commercial Research Purposes, distribution of a task-specific package containing one or more permitted Separable Adaptations, such as LoRA parameters together with a task-specific prediction head, provided that the package satisfies the requirements above and does not contain the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint or a substantial portion of its parameters.

A task-specific Output-Derived Model materially developed using Outputs or representations from a Restricted-Access Checkpoint may also be distributed for Non-Commercial Research Purposes, provided that:

(a) the Output-Derived Model does not incorporate, reproduce, or contain parameters of the Restricted-Access Checkpoint;

(b) the Output-Derived Model is designed for a specialized downstream task and is not intended to reproduce, approximate, substitute for, or materially replicate substantial general-purpose capabilities of RIBOSPAN;

(c) the distribution does not include substantial collections of Outputs prohibited under Section 11.5;

(d) the distributor clearly identifies that the model was materially developed using Outputs or representations generated by a Restricted-Access RIBOSPAN checkpoint;

(e) reasonable attribution to RIBOSPAN is provided;

(f) the distribution includes a copy of, or a clear reference to, this License, and access to or use of the Output-Derived Model is conditioned on the recipient's acceptance of the applicable terms of this License;

(g) recipients are clearly informed that Commercial Use requires separate written authorization from the Licensor; and

(h) the distribution otherwise complies with this License.

Recipients of Separable Adaptations or Output-Derived Models distributed in compliance with this Section may use, modify, fine-tune, and further redistribute such materials for Non-Commercial Research Purposes, provided that:

(a) the resulting materials continue to satisfy the applicable requirements of this Section;

(b) no Restricted-Access Checkpoint, full or self-contained Derivative Model based on such checkpoint, or substantial portion of the underlying checkpoint's parameters is redistributed;

(c) any person or entity requiring the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint obtains access to it independently in accordance with Section 11.2; and

(d) the recipient otherwise complies with this License.

Nothing in this Section permits a recipient of a Separable Adaptation or Output-Derived Model to obtain, reconstruct, receive, or access the underlying Restricted-Access Checkpoint through another user's account, credentials, authentication token, private link, access key, or other access mechanism.

Commercial Use of any Derivative Model, Separable Adaptation, adapter, LoRA parameters, parameter-efficient fine-tuning module, task-specific head, Output-Derived Model, or other adaptation materially developed from or using a Restricted-Access Checkpoint requires a separate written commercial license from the Licensor.

11.5 Systematic Distribution of Outputs

Except with prior written permission from the Licensor, you may not systematically publish, distribute, transfer, or otherwise make available substantial collections of Outputs generated using a Restricted-Access Checkpoint where such distribution would materially enable others to reproduce, approximate, substitute for, or bypass the access restrictions applicable to that checkpoint.

This Section does not restrict publication or distribution of reasonable portions of Outputs necessary to describe, evaluate, validate, or reproduce permitted Non-Commercial Research, including results reasonably necessary for scientific publications, benchmarks, supplementary materials, and research demonstrations.

11.6 Security

You must take reasonable technical and organizational measures to prevent unauthorized access to or redistribution of Restricted-Access Checkpoints.

